All three verbs are fixed, and committed as 1794cc06: yoyo docs, yoyo lint and yoyo skill now take one spaced argument whole, and an unknown yoyo lint subcommand exits 2. Build, the full cargo test, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check all pass. The harness hasn't pushed yet; I commented the before/after table on #1009 already, citing the sha.

| command | before | after |
|---|---|---|
| docs "a b" | ✗ Invalid crate name: '"a', exit 1 | ✗ Invalid crate name: 'a b', exit 1 |
| lint "a b" | Unknown /lint subcommand: "a b", exit 1 | Unknown /lint subcommand: a b, exit 2 |
| skill "a b" | unknown subcommand: "a b", exit 2 | unknown subcommand: a b, exit 2 |
| lint zzzq | exit 1 | exit 2, the usage-error code every other unknown subcommand uses |

One change outside the planned files. /docs splits its input on whitespace into a crate name and an item. The planned plain-join fix would have made yoyo docs "a b" look up crate a, item b on docs.rs. So I split handle_docs_status in src/commands_project.rs and added docs_lookup_status(crate, item). The shell docs command now passes the first argument straight in as the crate name, so "a b" is rejected whole, as cargo info "a b" does. The REPL /docs keeps its parsing and calls the same function. The file grows 7 lines; it was already over its recorded size limit, and the size test still passes. The commit body explains this.

Other changes:
• /lint and /skill never treat quotes specially, so they now get the plain join that outline and blame already use. As a side effect, skill show "my skill" and skill install "dir sp" now reach the handler without the literal quotes.
• Arguments without spaces pass through unchanged for all three commands.
• The existing unit test's expected exit code moved from 1 to 2, with a comment saying the change is on purpose. The exit-code line in docs/src/usage/commands.md now says 2.

Testing: a new integration test, docs_lint_skill_take_one_spaced_argv_element_whole, checks the exact refusal lines and that no " appears. It also pins the cases that must not change: bare lint still exits 1, lint fix 2, skill list 0, bare docs 2. The test failed before the fix. Restoring only src/dispatch_sub.rs to the previous version makes it fail again; putting the fix back makes it pass.

Two gaps:
• I didn't test a valid but nonexistent crate name like zz_not_a_crate_zz, because that needs a network call to docs.rs. The unspaced case uses an invalid name (zz@bad) instead, which is rejected offline.
• yoyo docs "" now prints Invalid crate name: '' and exits 1. Before, it printed usage and exited 2. Nothing pins this edge case.

Closing the issue: the remaining rows in #1009 (tree, undo, changelog, evolution) are marked "not observable" in its body, so "Fixes #1009" is accurate. The #1009 mentions left in src/ describe history in code comments; none of them point users at the ticket.

