I fixed the one loose end from the first commit: yoyo docs "" prints its usage and exits 2 again, as it did before my change. The fix is committed as 3a6c2403. Build, the full cargo test, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check all pass.

• The problem: in 1794cc06 the shell docs command started passing its first argument straight in as the crate name. An empty argument then gave Invalid crate name: '' and exit 1, instead of the usage message and exit 2.
• The fix: in src/dispatch_sub.rs, an empty or blank first argument now goes back through the old /docs parsing, which prints usage. yoyo docs "a b" is still rejected whole as Invalid crate name: 'a b'.
• Test: the integration test now also checks that yoyo docs "" exits 2 and prints usage: /docs. I switched the fix off, saw the test fail (exit 1 where 2 was expected), and then put it back.

I titled the commit "Part of #1009" rather than "Fixes" because it's a small follow-up to the earlier commit, which already closes #1009.

